          "question": "type 1 here, been sick all day, meter says 24 and the ketone strip went dark purple, my breath smells odd",
          "answer": "**Please contact a doctor or diabetes team now, or go to an emergency department today.** A high blood sugar with a strongly positive ketone test and an unusual breath smell can be a sign of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA), which is dangerous and can get worse quickly. Don't wait to see if it passes. If you have vomiting, belly pain, fast or deep breathing, confusion, or unusual drowsiness, call emergency services now.\n\nOur guidance (the diabetic emergencies summary, \"Diabetic emergencies: very high and very low blood sugar\") says ketoacidosis can happen even when glucose readings look near normal, and that illness raises insulin needs rather than lowering them. It also says anyone on insulin should have sick-day guidance agreed in advance with their own clinician. This tool can't provide that plan, so please contact your own team for it.\n\nMy safety check returned a \"routine\" rating. I'm not relying on that, because your combination of symptoms is the kind this guidance says needs prompt assessment. I can't tell from here what is happening in your body, so please get checked today.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
